From 628d1cb61dbe8bab72147b71098ea64685742b3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vibe Nuage Agent <vibe@mistral.ai>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:25:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Identify V1 InMotion wheels via the slow-info query instead
 of the board string

A V9 (and other V1-dialect wheels) answers the V2 identification probe only
with its board form-factor string ('Form V11 HMIC(0x21)'), which is not a
model identifier - latching the model from it misidentifies a V9 as a V11.

- Add the V1 slow-info request (WheelLog getSlowData: CAN 0x0F550114 remote
  frame) to the startup queries. The wheel answers with MAIN_INFO pages:
  car type (authoritative model), serial number and firmware version.
  Verified against a real V9 capture (series 12/type 1 -> V9).
- buildV1Frame now supports remote frames (type byte 1) used by the request.
- matchesCustomQueryResponse matches MAIN_INFO responses to the slow-info
  query so it completes and does not retry.
- Stop latching modelName from the legacy Form string (keep it only as a
  firmware hint); parseMainInfo's car-type page remains the model source.
- Tests: slow-info query exists, matches the captured car-type frame and
  latches 'InMotion V9'; the Form string matches the identification query
  without latching the model.
